  "title": "That Famous NASCAR Boom Tube Exhaust Sound Was an Accident",
  "summary": "The design of race car exhaust has been a fine science for decades, but few designs have been as notable—or have had the ear-splitting appeal—of the “boom tubes” of NASCAR stock cars in the early 2000s. The sound was actually a side effect, but when something hits the double-whammy of being both better and more […]",
